## Auto-write contracts

When an audit / skill / sub-ship surfaces an item below, the agent
MUST write the entry to the named ledger. Operator reviews at boundary;
agent does mechanical bookkeeping. Don't bury in chat / code comments
/ postmortems — those rotate or get compacted.

| Surface | Ledger | Trigger |
|---|---|---|
| Parity findings | `DOCS/PARITY_ISSUES.md` | `/parity-check` or any audit naming a parity surface |
| Deferred items | `DOCS/TECH_DEBT.md` | `/readiness` Check 25, `/merge-scan`, scope-discussion deferrals |
| Operator-visible features | `tick-trader-percore-workspace/FEATURE_LOOKUP.md` | New cfg flag / observability surface / persistence file / boot gate / training knob / fallback path at sub-ship close |
| Decoupling positioning | `plans/_future/2026-05-12-decoupling-endgoal-roadmap.md` | Any ship touching GUI ↔ runtime, TUISnapshot, CLI mode dispatch, cfg ownership, logging path |
| Cohort-audit findings | `DOCS/TECH_DEBT.md` | New boolean cfg field with 2+ siblings → cohort eligibility per `DESIGN_SPECS/cfg-flag-eligibility-criteria.md` |
| Operational landmines | `tick-trader-percore-workspace/DOCS/LANDMINES.md` | Non-obvious pitfall (segfault / race / library quirk) that took >1h to debug |

**FEATURE_LOOKUP entry template:** `### <name> (vX.Y.Z+)` → **What** /
**Cfg flags** / **Fallback** / **Where to verify** (panel field /
log line / file with file:line refs) / **Paper-test sanity** / **Gotchas** /
**Related**. Skip auto-write for: pure refactors, internal helper
extraction, bug fixes restoring expected behavior, bytewise-identical
perf optimizations.

